{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790453228,"nonce":"pB3aeZBfW5U3eKTJVFBIhN6aY3Q=","message":"wren-lift-dc (2026-09-26), wren_lift ae07899, not pushed: WrenLift's wasm native libraries follow Ash's side-module model (ash docs/wasm/hdlls.md). A library is a dylink.0 side module \u003clib\u003e.wasm beside the program, exporting its #! symbol functions as extern \"C\" fn(*mut VM) against wlift_abi. On a non-host build the runtime's foreign loader goes through env.ash_host_dlopen and env.ash_host_dlsym, reached by two function pointers that wlift_aot_set_native_loader(open, sym) sets. Only a WrenLift program with foreign classes installs them, so the runtime links alone and imports nothing new. The earlier entries (wlift_aot_set_plugin_dispatch, host_alloc/free, register_plugin_export) are gone. For caribou-wren hosting WrenLift foreign classes in its own program: call wlift_aot_set_native_loader with forwards to the same two imports.","files":null}]}